    "status": "draft",
    "summary": "Three consumer-visible inconsistencies survived 0.27.0, each documented in its handoff with a workaround. `check --json` and `index check --json` still report an unresolved claim as `fresh: false` with a `stale shard` line, where the human output and every other verb say validation, not staleness (spec 145). `index coverage`, `index owner`, `scope evaluate` and `registry show` print nothing on stdout under `--json` when they refuse, so a consumer gets an empty document where the verdict verbs give an error envelope. And a compact plan path refused for a `:` is told to drop `.`, `..` and a leading slash, none of which it has. This spec makes the index half of the JSON freshness report answer drift alone and carry the claims separately, gives every `--json` verb an error envelope on failure, and makes the compact refusal name the rule the path broke.\n",
    "title": "A refusal says what it is in every form"
  },
